meta {
  name: resend-verification-email
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseURL}}/auth/resend-verification-email
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "email": "pharmacist@example.com"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Resend Verification Email

  Sends a fresh verification email when an unverified account exists for the submitted address.

  ## Request Body

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  |-------|------|----------|-------------|
  | `email` | email string | Yes | Address to verify. |

  ## Success Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {
    "status": "success",
    "message": "Verification email sent successfully",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  ## Enumeration Protection

  The endpoint returns the same success response when:

  - no account exists for the email
  - the account is already verified
  - a new verification message was sent

  This prevents callers from discovering registered accounts through response differences.

  ## Side Effects for an Unverified Account

  - Replaces the previous verification-code record.
  - Sends a new verification email.
  - The old code can no longer be used.

  ## Errors

  | Status | Description |
  |--------|-------------|
  | `422 Unprocessable Entity` | The email is missing or invalid. |
  | `429 Too Many Requests` | Authentication rate limit was exceeded. |
  | `500 Internal Server Error` | Verification-code persistence or email delivery failed. |
}
